From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:21:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): add a project chip to the phone new-session
 landing

On phones the landing heading always reads "Start a new session in" and only
the icon changes with the project, so the selected project goes unnamed.
Choosing one also means finding + > Work in a project.

Lead the phone controls under the heading with a chip that names the project
(or "No project"). Its menu lists No project and every project with no search
field, so the keyboard stays down; the rows are radio items, so assistive tech
is told which one is selected. Picking one goes through the same
`?project=` switch as the + menu; No project removes only that parameter, and
the landing stays mounted so the draft is kept while the defaults reseed.
Desktop and Add nested agent are unchanged.

[Desidero: the test mocks routing without useReplaceSearchParams, which this
base does not have yet]

Not upstream yet: proposed from feat/mobile-landing-project-chip; drop this copy once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit fd40afd93398f12c6139c416ffb462618adb5c8f)
